>   (§3 of the note); let B♭ = (b♭_1, …, b♭_m) on Z_{n♭}, n♭ | n, be the multiset at which this stops. Then (1) every
>   signing ε that is good for B♭ on Z_{n♭} is good for B on Z_n (the same ε: the k-th element keeps its sign), by
>   Lemma 2 at each step; (2) for every prime p | n♭, every level 1, …, v_p(n♭) of the p-tree of B♭ has a full group:
>   a level that is not contractible has, by the definition, a group that holds an element and has no empty subclass
>   (§3: "In the last multiset no level of any tree is contractible: at every level i of every p-tree some group has
